  "context": "Prioritize principled Bayesian methodology and statistical computation for complex data: variational inference, expectation propagation, MCMC, scalability, convergence and approximate inference. Favor latent-structure models, generalized linear mixed models, dynamic and state-space models, and network models, especially contributions combining theory and computation. Nonparametric Bayes, survival analysis and spatial statistics are secondary interests when connected to these themes. Give lower priority to deep learning, reinforcement learning or graph neural networks without substantial statistical methodology, routine applications, and software-only descriptions without a methodological contribution.",
